    <node id="INFECTIONS">
      <data key="d0">INFECTIONS</data>
      <data key="d1">INFECTIONS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Infections are illnesses caused by pathogens, and they are commonly included in family history questions as part of medical assessments. In the context of cancer treatment, infections are also a frequent side effect of targeted therapy, and the body becomes particularly vulnerable to infections during high-dose chemotherapy. Thus, infections represent both a general category of disease and a specific clinical concern for patients undergoing certain cancer treatments.
Relationships:
  - None recorded in the provided Relationships table.</data>
