    <node id="RADIOLOGIST">
      <data key="d0">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d1">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A radiologist is a physician (doctor) who specializes in interpreting medical imaging tests. They are experts in reading and analyzing images from a wide range of modalities, including MRI, CT, PET, ultrasound, and bone scans, as well as diagnostic mammograms. In some settings, a radiologist evaluates diagnostic mammograms while the patient waits. They study the images carefully, write a detailed report of their findings, and send the results to the patient’s doctor, health care provider, or care team—such as an oncologist. Some radiologists have particular expertise in imaging the nervous system, reviewing MRI or CT images of the brain and spine and conveying results to the care team. Overall, the radiologist serves as a diagnostic expert who bridges imaging technology and clinical care, ensuring that referring physicians receive accurate interpretations to guide patient treatment.
Relationships:
  - Source: RADIOLOGIST
    Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
    Description: The radiologist writes an imaging report following an examination and sends it to the patient's health care provider. This report is a formal documentation of the radiologist's findings and interpretations. The health care provider receives this imaging report to inform patient care decisions. Thus, the radiologist and the health care provider are connected through the delivery of the written imaging report, ensuring that diagnostic information reaches the provider responsible for the patient's treatment.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
