    <node id="PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN">
      <data key="d0">PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN</data>
      <data key="d1">PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">The primary care physician (PCP) is the patient’s main and regular doctor, playing a central role in ongoing care. The PCP is considered a partner in the patient’s care and should be kept informed about any changes to the care team contact list, as well as any updates regarding the patient’s health, treatment, and important dates. In addition to providing general medical care, the PCP is often the first health care professional to evaluate people who have symptoms of anal cancer. Overall, the PCP serves as a key point of contact and coordinator within the patient’s broader health care team.
Relationships: None listed in the relationships table.</data>
    </node>
