      <data key="d1">TREATMENT TEAM</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">(No description provided in the data)
Relationships:
  - Source: TREATMENT TEAM
    Target: BIOPSY
    Description: The treatment team uses biopsy results to figure out the best treatment plan.
  - Source: BIOPSY
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team reviews prior biopsy results and tumor tissue
  - Source: TREATMENT TEAM
    Target: CHEMOTHERAPY
    Description: The treatment team helps the patient prevent or lessen side effects caused by chemotherapy.
  - Source: CHEMOTHERAPY
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team explains how often, how long, and how chemotherapy is given and its side effects
  - Source: CANCER TREATMENT
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team provides and coordinates cancer care, including distress screening as part of cancer care.
  - Source: SURGERY
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team reviews prior surgery and testing results
  - Source: RADIATION THERAPY
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Patients should talk to their treatment team about the benefits of radiation therapy compared with the risk of nervous system damage
  - Source: PATIENT
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team screens the patient's level of distress and provides cancer care
  - Source: OVARIAN CANCER
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team plans and coordinates ovarian cancer treatment
  - Source: TREATMENT TEAM
    Target: DOCTOR
    Description: The doctor is part of the patient's treatment team.
  - Source: TREATMENT TEAM
    Target: PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA
    Description: The treatment team manages treatment for primary CNS lymphoma
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIALS
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Patients are told to ask their treatment team whether they meet the requirements for a clinical trial.
  - Source: STEM CELL RESCUE
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team considers many factors to decide if a stem cell rescue is right for a patient
  - Source: NEUROSURGEON
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The neurosurgeon is part of the medical team that uses diagnostic information to plan treatment.
  - Source: FERTILITY PRESERVATION
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Patients are advised to ask their care team about fertility changes and referrals to fertility specialists for preservation options before treatment.
  - Source: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Neuropathologist findings and diagnostic information help the treatment team plan treatment.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Histology helps classify the tumor and contributes to the full description used to plan treatment.
  - Source: LABORATORY
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Laboratory results from biopsy analysis are used by the treatment team to plan treatment.
  - Source: ADVANCED-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: A treatment team works with the patient to choose the best treatments for advanced-stage prostate cancer.
  - Source: LAB TESTING
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team uses lab testing information to plan treatment.
  - Source: MOLECULAR TESTING
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: Molecular testing results help the treatment team identify tumor type and growth rate to plan treatment.
  - Source: NUTRITION ASSESSMENT
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The treatment team monitors the patient for weight loss and other signs of inadequate nutrition during and after treatment.
  - Source: TREATMENT TEAM
    Target: HAND-FOOT SYNDROME
    Description: The treatment team is involved in managing side effects such as hand-foot syndrome.
  - Source: HEPATITIS B AND HEPATITIS C SCREENING
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: The hepatitis blood test tells the treatment team whether the patient has or had hepatitis B or C.
  - Source: CANCER DIAGNOSIS
    Target: TREATMENT TEAM
    Description: After a cancer diagnosis, the treatment team screens distress as part of the patient's cancer care.

---

