      <data key="d3">MASTECTOMY is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of all or part of the breast. It is primarily performed as an operation to treat cancer, though it may also be used in preventive or other medical contexts. The procedure encompasses both total removal of the breast tissue and partial removal, depending on the extent of the disease and the treatment plan.
