      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">TNM staging is a classification method that scores Tumor (T), Node (N), and Metastasis (M) to help assign a cancer stage.

**Relationships:**
  - Source: TNM STAGING
  - Target: CANCER STAGING
  - Description: Cancer staging uses TNM staging scores to assign a cancer stage.

  - Source: TNM STAGING
  - Target: METASTASIS
  - Description: Metastasis is one of the three components scored in TNM staging. TNM staging includes the M category to indicate whether cancer has metastasized.

---</data>
