      <data key="d6">10. **Relationship id 789:** Source: NCCN CANCER CENTERS → Target: NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE — "The National Cancer Institute (NCI) and NCCN Cancer Centers are both U.S. organizations listed as resources for finding cancer clinical trials. They serve as authoritative sources for locating clinical trials available in the United States. NCCN Cancer Centers can be accessed online at NCCN.org/cancercenters, while the NCI’s corresponding resource is available at cancer.gov. Both are recognized for providing information on cancer clinical trials to patients, caregivers, and researchers."</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RELATIONSHIP ID 2525: SOURCE: NCCN CANCER CENTERS → TARGET: U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE — &quot;NCCN CANCER CENTERS AND THE U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM) ARE BOTH RECOGNIZED RESOURCES FOR LOCATING CLINICAL TRIALS. NCCN CANCER CENTERS ARE SPECIFICALLY LISTED AS A RESOURCE FOR FINDING CLINICAL TRIALS WITHIN THE UNITED STATES, WHILE THE NLM PROVIDES THE WORLDWIDE CLINICALTRIALS.GOV DATABASE. TOGETHER, THESE TWO ENTITIES OFFER COMPLEMENTARY ACCESS TO CLINICAL TRIAL INFORMATION: NCCN CANCER CENTERS FOCUS ON U.S.-BASED CANCER CENTERS, AND THE NLM SUPPLIES A COMPREHENSIVE, GLOBAL DATABASE OF CLINICAL TRIALS.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">RELATIONSHIP ID 2525: SOURCE: NCCN CANCER CENTERS → TARGET: U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE — "NCCN CANCER CENTERS AND THE U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM) ARE BOTH RECOGNIZED RESOURCES FOR LOCATING CLINICAL TRIALS. NCCN CANCER CENTERS ARE SPECIFICALLY LISTED AS A RESOURCE FOR FINDING CLINICAL TRIALS WITHIN THE UNITED STATES, WHILE THE NLM PROVIDES THE WORLDWIDE CLINICALTRIALS.GOV DATABASE. TOGETHER, THESE TWO ENTITIES OFFER COMPLEMENTARY ACCESS TO CLINICAL TRIAL INFORMATION: NCCN CANCER CENTERS FOCUS ON U.S.-BASED CANCER CENTERS, AND THE NLM SUPPLIES A COMPREHENSIVE, GLOBAL DATABASE OF CLINICAL TRIALS."</data>
      <data key="d1">RELATIONSHIP ID 2525: SOURCE: NCCN CANCER CENTERS → TARGET: U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE — "NCCN CANCER CENTERS AND THE U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM) ARE BOTH RECOGNIZED RESOURCES FOR LOCATING CLINICAL TRIALS. NCCN CANCER CENTERS ARE SPECIFICALLY LISTED AS A RESOURCE FOR FINDING CLINICAL TRIALS WITHIN THE UNITED STATES, WHILE THE NLM PROVIDES THE WORLDWIDE CLINICALTRIALS.GOV DATABASE. TOGETHER, THESE TWO ENTITIES OFFER COMPLEMENTARY ACCESS TO CLINICAL TRIAL INFORMATION: NCCN CANCER CENTERS FOCUS ON U.S.-BASED CANCER CENTERS, AND THE NLM SUPPLIES A COMPREHENSIVE, GLOBAL DATABASE OF CLINICAL TRIALS."</data>
