      <data key="d6"> Source: NCCN CANCER CENTERS → Target: CLINICAL TRIAL — "NCCN Cancer Centers serve as a key resource for identifying and accessing clinical trials. These centers are formally recognized as a U.S.-based resource for individuals seeking information about clinical trial opportunities. The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) Cancer Centers provide a curated listing that helps patients, caregivers, and healthcare professionals locate relevant clinical trials across the United States. By utilizing these centers, users can connect with ongoing research studies and potentially participate in the advancement of cancer treatment. The entity "NCCN CANCER CENTERS" is thus directly associated with the facilitation of "CLINICAL TRIAL" discovery. Together, the descriptions emphasize that NCCN Cancer Centers are a reliable, U.S.-specific source for finding clinical trials, offering a centralized approach to navigating the complex landscape of cancer research."</data>
    </node>
