      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6"> Source: NCCN CANCER CENTERS → Target: U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE — "NCCN Cancer Centers and the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) are both recognized resources for locating clinical trials. NCCN Cancer Centers are specifically listed as a resource for finding clinical trials within the United States, while the NLM provides the worldwide clinicaltrials.gov database. Together, these two entities offer complementary access to clinical trial information: NCCN Cancer Centers focus on U.S.-based cancer centers, and the NLM supplies a comprehensive, global database of clinical trials."

---

**Summary:** The dataset contains 20 entities in the Entities table (plus 4 relationship-only entities) and 11 relationship records. None of these records names a specific member institution of the NCCN Cancer Centers network; the network is characterized only as an NCCN-affiliated, U.S.-based group of cancer centers listed at NCCN.org/cancercenters that helps patients find clinical trials [Data: Entities (205, 417, 0); Relationships (380, 2526, 799, 790, 788, 789, 2525, +more)].</data>
    </node>
