    <node id="HPV VACCINATION">
      <data key="d0">HPV VACCINATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HPV VACCINATION</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">HPV vaccination is the administration of a vaccine that protects against HPV strains, including the highest-risk strains; it can prevent new HPV infections but does not treat existing HPV infection or HPV-related cancer.
Relationships:
  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Target: HPV VACCINATION
  - Description: By preventing HPV infection, HPV vaccination can reduce the risk of HPV-related cervical cancer.
  - Source: UNITED STATES
  - Target: HPV VACCINATION
  - Description: The 9-strain HPV vaccine is available in the United States and vaccination is an option for adults aged 45 and under.
  - Source: HPV
  - Target: HPV VACCINATION
  - Description: The HPV vaccine prevents new HPV infections.</data>
