    <node id="COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL">
      <data key="d0">COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL</data>
      <data key="d1">COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The Comprehensive Metabolic Panel (CMP) is a blood test that measures a variety of substances in the blood to provide detailed information about kidney and liver function. It serves as a screening tool for up to 14 different chemicals, helping to assess overall metabolic health. In particular, the CMP evaluates markers related to kidney function, liver function, and includes measurements such as calcium levels. By analyzing these substances, the test aids in detecting, diagnosing, or monitoring conditions affecting the kidneys and liver, as well as broader metabolic imbalances.
Relationships:
  - Source: CLL
    Target: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
    Description: Comprehensive metabolic panel is a test used to plan CLL treatment.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
Description: The Comprehensive Metabolic Panel (CMP) is a blood test that measures a variety of substances in the blood to provide detailed information about kidney and liver function. It serves as a screening tool for up to 14 different chemicals, helping to assess overall metabolic health. In particular, the CMP evaluates markers related to kidney function, liver function, and includes measurements such as calcium levels. By analyzing these substances, the test aids in detecting, diagnosing, or monitoring conditions affecting the kidneys and liver, as well as broader metabolic imbalances.
Relationships:
  - Source: CLL
    Target: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
    Description: Comprehensive metabolic panel is a test used to plan CLL treatment.</data>
    </node>
