    <node id="FLOW CYTOMETRY">
      <data key="d0">FLOW CYTOMETRY</data>
      <data key="d1">FLOW CYTOMETRY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Flow cytometry is a laboratory test used in the diagnosis and treatment planning of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). It is a laboratory method designed to detect, identify, and count specific cells, and it can be performed on cells from peripheral blood or bone marrow aspirates. Flow cytometry is commonly used for immunophenotyping, which helps characterize cell types based on surface markers.
Relationships:
  - Source: CLL
    Target: FLOW CYTOMETRY
    Description: Flow cytometry is a test used to plan CLL treatment.</data>
