    <node id="PATIENTS ABOUT TO UNDERGO CANCER TREATMENT. THE SCREENING RELATIONSHIP TO CANCER TREATMENT STATES: &quot;SCREENING IS NEEDED BECAUSE SOME CANCER TREATMENTS CAN REACTIVATE HEPATITIS B OR HEPATITIS C AND CAUSE LIVER DAMAGE&quot; [DATA: RELATIONSHIPS (1062); SOURCES (84)].">
      <data key="d0">PATIENTS ABOUT TO UNDERGO CANCER TREATMENT. THE SCREENING RELATIONSHIP TO CANCER TREATMENT STATES: "SCREENING IS NEEDED BECAUSE SOME CANCER TREATMENTS CAN REACTIVATE HEPATITIS B OR HEPATITIS C AND CAUSE LIVER DAMAGE" [DATA: RELATIONSHIPS (1062); SOURCES (84)].</data>
      <data key="d1">PATIENTS ABOUT TO UNDERGO CANCER TREATMENT. THE SCREENING RELATIONSHIP TO CANCER TREATMENT STATES: "SCREENING IS NEEDED BECAUSE SOME CANCER TREATMENTS CAN REACTIVATE HEPATITIS B OR HEPATITIS C AND CAUSE LIVER DAMAGE" [DATA: RELATIONSHIPS (1062); SOURCES (84)].</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">2. **Patients with chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL).** Hepatitis B and C testing is explicitly performed before CLL treatment, and hepatitis B is described as a *required* screening test before CLL treatment due to the risk of viral reactivation during immunosuppressive therapy; hepatitis C is likewise specifically tested for before CLL treatment begins [Data: Entities (245, 246); Relationships (467); Sources (30)].</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATIENTS UNDERGOING TREATMENT PLANNING GENERALLY. SCREENING FOR HEPATITIS B IS LISTED AS AN AS-NEEDED PART OF TREATMENT PLANNING, AND THE RESULTING HEPATITIS BLOOD TEST INFORMS THE TREATMENT TEAM WHETHER THE PATIENT HAS OR HAD HEPATITIS B OR C [DATA: RELATIONSHIPS (1061, 2156); SOURCES (159, 84)].">
      <data key="d0">PATIENTS UNDERGOING TREATMENT PLANNING GENERALLY. SCREENING FOR HEPATITIS B IS LISTED AS AN AS-NEEDED PART OF TREATMENT PLANNING, AND THE RESULTING HEPATITIS BLOOD TEST INFORMS THE TREATMENT TEAM WHETHER THE PATIENT HAS OR HAD HEPATITIS B OR C [DATA: RELATIONSHIPS (1061, 2156); SOURCES (159, 84)].</data>
      <data key="d1">PATIENTS UNDERGOING TREATMENT PLANNING GENERALLY. SCREENING FOR HEPATITIS B IS LISTED AS AN AS-NEEDED PART OF TREATMENT PLANNING, AND THE RESULTING HEPATITIS BLOOD TEST INFORMS THE TREATMENT TEAM WHETHER THE PATIENT HAS OR HAD HEPATITIS B OR C [DATA: RELATIONSHIPS (1061, 2156); SOURCES (159, 84)].</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">
More broadly, hepatitis B and hepatitis C are themselves significant because they can cause chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer — the underlying rationale for screening before immunosuppressive or hepatotoxic cancer therapy [Data: Entities (245, 246); Relationships (735, 738, 736, 739, 737, 740); Sources (51, 84)].

---
</data>
