    <node id="PD-L1 TESTING">
      <data key="d0">PD-L1 TESTING</data>
      <data key="d1">PD-L1 TESTING</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">PD-L1 testing is a biomarker test used to measure the expression of programmed death ligand 1 (PD-L1) on cancer cells. It checks for the presence of PD-L1, a protein that cancer cells can express to evade immune detection, in order to guide the use of immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy. The test quantifies PD-L1 expression using a combined positive score (CPS), which assesses the number of PD-L1-positive cells relative to viable tumor cells. As a diagnostic tool, PD-L1 testing is designed to help activate the immune system to fight cancer by identifying patients who are most likely to benefit from immune checkpoint inhibitors, thereby informing treatment decisions.  
Relationships: None listed in the Relationships table.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: PD-L1 TESTING
Description: PD-L1 testing is a biomarker test used to measure the expression of programmed death ligand 1 (PD-L1) on cancer cells. It checks for the presence of PD-L1, a protein that cancer cells can express to evade immune detection, in order to guide the use of immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy. The test quantifies PD-L1 expression using a combined positive score (CPS), which assesses the number of PD-L1-positive cells relative to viable tumor cells. As a diagnostic tool, PD-L1 testing is designed to help activate the immune system to fight cancer by identifying patients who are most likely to benefit from immune checkpoint inhibitors, thereby informing treatment decisions.  
Relationships: None listed in the Relationships table.</data>
    </node>
