      <data key="d6">
The supporting laboratory infrastructure is also present: BLOOD TEST is "a laboratory procedure in which a needle is inserted into a vein to collect a blood sample," and the sample is examined in a lab [Data: Entities (558, 727); Relationships (1682)].

It is important to note that in this dataset the entity HEPATITIS itself is **not** directly connected to any laboratory test in the relationship graph. Its direct links are to disease outcomes and categories: HEPATITIS is "a recognized risk factor for the development of liver cancer," can cause liver failure, and is "a type of liver disease"; its viral subtypes HEPATITIS B and HEPATITIS C are the ones that connect to the blood tests, and they can cause chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer [Data: Entities (384, 245, 246); Relationships (717, 733, 734, 731, 732, 735, 738, 736, 739, 737, 740, 741, 742)].

LIVER FUNCTION TESTS are blood tests measuring chemicals and enzymes made or processed by the liver, with abnormal levels indicating liver damage; however, they are not directly linked to HEPATITIS by any relationship in this graph — they connect instead to BLOOD TESTS and the CARE TEAM [Data: Entities (491); Relationships (981, 1000)].

---
</data>
