      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Fine-needle biopsy (FNB) is a needle-based biopsy procedure that uses a needle to remove a sample of tissue from a tumor or lymph node. It can be guided by imaging techniques such as ultrasound or computed tomography (CT) to ensure accurate placement of the needle.
Relationships: None in the provided Relationships table.</data>
