    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="HEALTH CARE PROVIDER" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">HEALTH CARE PROVIDER</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The radiologist writes an imaging report following an examination and sends it to the patient's health care provider. This report is a formal documentation of the radiologist's findings and interpretations. The health care provider receives this imaging report to inform patient care decisions. Thus, the radiologist and the health care provider are connected through the delivery of the written imaging report, ensuring that diagnostic information reaches the provider responsible for the patient's treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">HEALTH CARE PROVIDER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist evaluates the diagnostic mammogram while the patient waits</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="MRI" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">MRI</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The radiologist studies MRI images after the scan is performed.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="CARE TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The radiologist plays a key supportive role within the broader care team by performing and interpreting imaging tests. Once the radiologist has analyzed the images, they send the imaging results directly to the care teamspecifically to the referring doctor or physicianto ensure that the findings are communicated clearly and promptly. This transmission of results is essential for helping the care team plan next steps in patient management, as it provides the diagnostic information needed to make informed decisions about treatment and follow-up care. By delivering accurate and timely interpretations, the radiologist supports the doctor and the entire care team in delivering effective, coordinated patient care.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="BIOPSY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist's interpretation of an image showing a possible glioma can lead to a biopsy.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="IMAGING" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">IMAGING</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The radiologist is an expert in analyzing images from nervous-system imaging tests.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="ULTRASOUND" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in interpreting imaging tests, including ultrasound. In this role, the radiologist reads and interprets ultrasound images to assist in diagnosing and monitoring medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="IMAGING TESTS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">IMAGING TESTS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist is a medical expert who specializes in reading imaging tests and studying the images they produce. The radiologist interprets the images generated by imaging tests, using their specialized expertise to analyze and understand the visual information captured. In this role, the radiologist serves as the key professional responsible for examining imaging test results and providing accurate interpretations of what the images reveal.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="CT SCAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">CT SCAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in interpreting diagnostic imaging. In the context of a CT scan, the radiologist reads and interprets CT images after the scan is performed. The radiologists role includes studying the resulting CT images and interpreting imaging tests such as CT scans to provide diagnostic information.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="DOCTOR" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">DOCTOR</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The radiologist is responsible for interpreting medical imaging and then communicating the findings to the referring doctor. This communication takes the form of a detailed report, which is sent directly to the doctor. Alongside the written report, the radiologist also sends the actual imaging results to the doctor. These imaging results, together with the report, are intended to help the doctor plan the next steps of the patient's care. Thus, the radiologist provides both the diagnostic interpretation and the supporting visual data, enabling the doctor to make informed decisions about treatment and follow-up.</data>
      <data key="d12">DOCTOR</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="PET SCAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">PET SCAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in interpreting imaging tests, including positron emission tomography (PET) scans. The radiologist reads and analyzes PET images to provide diagnostic information that helps guide patient care. PET scans are a form of nuclear medicine imaging that produce detailed images of functional processes in the body, and the radiologist plays a key role in interpreting these images to identify abnormalities and support clinical decisions.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="MRI SCAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">MRI SCAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in reading and interpreting imaging tests, including MRI scans. The radiologist examines MRI images to provide diagnostic information that helps guide patient care.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIOLOGIST" target="IMAGING TEST" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d8">IMAGING TEST</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A radiologist is an expert in reading imaging tests and interpreting the images they produce.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIOLOGIST</data>
    </edge>
