    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="NCCN CANCER CENTERS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The NCCN Cancer Centers serve as a key resource for locating clinical trials, specifically within the United States. These centers assist patients in identifying and accessing clinical trial opportunities, making them a valuable source of information for those seeking participation in research studies. The entity CLINICAL TRIAL is central to this resource, as the primary function of the NCCN Cancer Centers is to connect individuals with relevant clinical trials. In summary, NCCN Cancer Centers provide a United Statesbased resource dedicated to helping patients find clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Joining a clinical trial is a recommended option for treating primary CNS lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="CARE TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team plays a key role in evaluating whether a clinical trial is appropriate for a patient. They can be consulted directly to determine if a clinical trial might be right for the individual. To make this determination, the care team uses the patient's performance status as a key factor in assessing eligibility for a clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIALS" target="NCCN CANCER CENTERS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCCN Cancer Centers are listed as a resource for finding clinical trials in the United States</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIALS" target="TREATMENT TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d8">TREATMENT TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Patients are told to ask their treatment team whether they meet the requirements for a clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d12">TREATMENT TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIALS" target="CARE TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The clinical trials process is closely coordinated with the patients care team. Patients are advised to ask their care team about access to clinical trials, and the care team plays a central role in facilitating clinical trial participation. In this capacity, the care team also advises the patient on whether a clinical trial might be right for them, helping to guide the decision-making process. Together, these responsibilities ensure that patients receive personalized support and clear information when considering clinical trial options.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIALS" target="MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d8">MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The MDT makes treatment decisions and can consider clinical trials as part of a patient's treatment plan</data>
      <data key="d12">MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM</data>
    </edge>
