    <edge source="CERVICAL CANCER" target="SURGERY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CERVICAL CANCER</data>
      <data key="d8">SURGERY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Cervical cancer is a disease in which malignant cells form in the tissues of the cervix. Surgery is a treatment option for cervical cancer and is particularly effective in the early stages of the disease. In fact, surgery is often the main treatment for early-stage cervical cancer, offering a primary approach to removing the cancerous tissue. Together, these statements underscore that surgical intervention plays a key role in managing cervical cancer, especially when the cancer has not spread extensively. The use of surgery is thus most commonly recommended for patients diagnosed at an early stage, where it can serve as a definitive treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">SURGERY</data>
    </edge>
