      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The multidisciplinary team (MDT) and the care team refer to the same group of professionals. This team is composed of both health care and psychosocial care professionals who work together in a unified manner. Their primary role is to plan and implement the patient's treatment. In essence, the care team is the multidisciplinary team, and the multidisciplinary team is the care teamtwo names for one collaborative unit dedicated to coordinating and delivering comprehensive patient care.</data>
